==Evolution==
Evolves into '''GENERAL MORDEN''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''GOLDEN MORDEN CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
DONALD MORDEN is an alright Crowd-Controller with some pretty decent stats to boot. Since it also has higher range than Special or Rare Alien knockbackers, it can target enemies like [[Ursamajor]], [[Maawth]] and [[I.M. Phace]]. Its niche of knocking back Aliens is not the best though, since on Alien-dominant stages, it will cause your other Cats to push into the range of backliners and get killed. It doesn't have much usage as a generalist sadly, since its stats are similar to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], with the exception of its notably lower range. If you have [[Mizli (Uber Rare Cat)|Mizli]], she'll likely be more useful because of her Warp Immunity and Slow ability, on top of her significantly lower recharge.

==='''True Form'''===
DONALD MORDEN finally differentiates itself from Mizuririn by gaining an extra target trait. Although another anti-Traitless Cat is great, it is mostly outclassed by [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], who has a faster recharge, Freeze and many immunities. For this reason, it likely won't be too useful unless Tourist Cat is outranged by a Traitless enemy, or playing on a stage combining Traitless and Alien threats, where its Area Attacks allow it to attack clusters of them with little worry.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Tanker}}

